# armour/shared/pauldron_plate4_r: the LARGE plate pauldron on the right shoulder (plate.4; LADDER-ARMOUR, STYLE_P2 25.6,
# 27.4): the medium cop a pixel broader and a lame deeper, 3 px past the shoulder line (the Heartland's shoulders from its
# first alloy: T4-T6); the cop lit at its top-left with one step-4 ridge pixel (its glint), two lames below the seam.
# It rides the lean and the bob and lifts a pixel on wind-ups (`up`). Finish regions: R the lower lame's hem, P the cop's
# face, N the seams, W a spot on the shadow side. Shared by both bodies. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# (LADDER-ARMOUR i3) D U and the near side view redrawn: a raised haute-piece (the neck flange, R: gilt from T3) over the domed
# cop and a lit lame, inside the old box (origin a row lower for the flange); N dropped (runes live on the breastplate).
use person
role pauldron plate.4
layer armNear
anchor shoulderR
keys pauld
z 5
side R

